AB  - Conventional loan approval systems are based either on rule-based systems that are rigid and inflexible or on machine learning models that are opaque, incomprehensible, and inaccessible. This paper describes a Policy-Aware Agentic AI Framework for Explainable Loan Decisioning that combines predictive modeling, financial behavior analysis, dynamic eligibility assessment, and multilingual user interaction. A stacked ensemble model predicts the probability of loan approval, and SHAP-based explainability provides a ranking of feature contributions to determine the most important drivers of decision-making. To ensure policy compliance, a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) component dynamically retrieves eligibility criteria from policy documents and assesses the compliance of applicants with a generalized compliance engine. A supervisor agent coordinates predictive, behavioral, and policy-level information to produce structured decisions that are classified as approval, conditional approval, and rejection, along with individualized recourse and government scheme recommendations. To promote financial inclusion, the system provides multilingual explanation delivery, allowing applicants to obtain decisions and recommendations in their language of choice. Experimental results show enhanced interpretability, policy compliance, and accessibility over machine learning models.
