AB  - This paper presents the design, fine-tuning, and evaluation of the Intelligent Khmer Audio-Based Learning and Conversational Tutoring System, named "InnerEcho," a fully locally deployed, voice-first bilingual AI tutoring platform for Cambodian Grade 12 students preparing for the National High School Examination (Baccauréat II). The system integrates three core trained model components: Whisper Small Khmer V2, a fine-tuned automatic speech recognition model based on the Whisper Small architecture (242M parameters) achieving a word error rate of 6.8% and character error rate of 3.1% on Khmer educational speech; MMS-TTS Khmer (facebook/mms-tts-khm), Meta’s Massively Multilingual Speech text-to-speech model further adapted on 200 hours of Khmer teacher voice data recorded at 16 kHz, attaining a Mean Opinion Score of 4.3 out of 5.0 and pronunciation accuracy of 91.4%; and a locally trained Retrieval-Augmented Generation pipeline comprising a fine-tuned multilingual BERT encoder (178M parameters) and a QLoRA-adapted LLaMA-3-8B generator trained on 12,800 curriculum-aligned Khmer question-answer pairs. A structured two-branch data preprocessing pipeline, a layer-freezing and fine-tuning strategy for TTS adaptation, and a freeze-layer and fine-tuning workflow for STT adaptation are described and evaluated. The integrated system achieves a retrieval Recall@5 of 97.4%, a hallucination rate of 1.2%, and a quiz accuracy of 94.1% against official Bac II answer keys, with end-to-end AI processing latency below 3.5 seconds. All model weights, training scripts, and curated datasets are released as open-source contributions.
